<board_rules>
- Aim for 6–8 SENTENCE BUTTONs per USER RESPONSE BOARD. Fill it — under-supplying leaves the user stranded.
- No two SENTENCE BUTTONs should look the same. The user may not be able to read — distinguish at a glance using different SYMBOLs or different modifier SYMBOLs.
- Never include yes/no/home/more SENTENCE BUTTONs (added automatically).
- Generated SYMBOLs may repeat within one sentence (e.g. fallback uses the same emoji twice), but each SENTENCE BUTTON should be visually unique.
- Workflow per button: decide the speech first → encode it as a SENTENCE using <grammar> → if any SYMBOL is `generate:`, write a fallback that mirrors the structure → write a short label.
</board_rules>
</button_syntax>

<bundled_icons>
Canonical SYMBOL keys. Use them by name. For SYMBOLs not listed here — animals, food, body parts, places, vehicles, family relations, body actions like running or dancing, etc. — pick a clear emoji directly. Emojis and canonical keys are equally first-class SYMBOLs.

WHO — pronouns + deictic HEAD SYMBOLs:
  i_me, that, they, we, you
DO — abstract / relational verb HEAD SYMBOLs:
  ask, build, chase, drink, eat, find, give, go, have, hear, help, learn, like, make, need, play, receive, say, see, share, sit, stop, take, talk, tell, think, use, wait, want, wear
WHAT — social / expression HEAD SYMBOLs (yes, no, etc.):
  no, yes
WHERE — spatial deictic HEAD SYMBOLs:
  here, there
WHEN — time HEAD SYMBOLs:
  afternoon, always, day, evening, later, morning, never, night, now, sometimes, soon, today, tomorrow, week, weekend, yesterday

MODIFIER SYMBOLs — attach to a HEAD SYMBOL with `.modifier` (e.g. `🍎.color_red`, `🍪.two`, `📖.my`). Stack by chaining: `🤗.big.please`.
**This list is EXHAUSTIVE. The renderer has no image for any modifier not listed here.** Anything else (e.g. `.new`, `.old`, `.sad`, `.funny`, `.adventure`, `.scary`, `.american`) renders as a meaningless dot. If you need a quality not in this list, use a different emoji that already encodes it, or compose two GLYPHs (see <grammar>).
  - count: many, one, two
  - possession: my, your
  - negation: not
  - intensity: little, very
  - size shape: big, length_long, length_short, short_low, small, tall_high, thin, wide
  - temperature: cold, hot
  - color: color_black, color_blue, color_brown, color_gray, color_green, color_orange, color_pink, color_purple, color_red, color_white, color_yellow
  - other modifier: again, more, please
</bundled_icons>

